# Line endings, fixed for every platform.
#
# Without this, what git stores depends on each machine's `core.autocrlf`, so a
# Windows checkout differs from a Linux CI checkout byte for byte — which shows
# up as whole-file diffs and, on Windows, as "LF will be replaced by CRLF"
# warnings on every commit.
#
# `text=auto` keeps git's own binary detection (images, app icons, the .webp
# screenshots are left alone) and `eol=lf` pins both what is stored and what is
# checked out to LF. Only line endings are affected — no file content is
# rewritten here, and existing files are normalised as they are next committed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows command scripts must keep CRLF: cmd.exe mis-parses an LF-only .bat.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
